mage-office: keep the exports pthread workers need in an optimized (ASSERTIONS=0) link.

Emscripten 3.1.65 requires _embind_initialize_bindings and _emscripten_thread_crashed for
pthreads, but an optimizing link without ASSERTIONS removes exports that are not in
EXPORTED_FUNCTIONS, so every worker died with "__embind_initialize_bindings is not defined".

diff --git a/desktop/util/Executable_soffice_bin-emscripten-exports b/desktop/util/Executable_soffice_bin-emscripten-exports
index 2206ccc..2073ab5 100644
--- a/desktop/util/Executable_soffice_bin-emscripten-exports
+++ b/desktop/util/Executable_soffice_bin-emscripten-exports
@@ -12,3 +12,7 @@ _lok_preinit
 _lok_preinit_2
 _malloc
 _free
+# mage-office: the pthread worker calls these by name (runtime_pthread.js); without ASSERTIONS the
+# optimizing link drops every export not listed here, and each worker then fails as it starts.
+__embind_initialize_bindings
+__emscripten_thread_crashed
